      "css": ".ds-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:2px 10px;border-radius:9999px;font:600 0.7rem/1.5 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap}.ds-badge-koreader{background:#d1fae5;color:#065f46;border:1px solid #a7f3d0}.ds-badge-readwise{background:#dbeafe;color:#1e40af;border:1px solid #bfdbfe}.ds-badge-manual{background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fde68a}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sidebar Nav Item",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-item",
      "description": "Sidebar row: emoji icon, 14px medium label, 8px radius. Active row fills with the deepest surface step and goes semibold.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-nav-shell\"><a class=\"ds-nav ds-nav-active\" href=\"#\"><span>&#128221;</span>Highlights</a><a class=\"ds-nav\" href=\"#\"><span>&#127991;&#65039;</span>Tags</a></div>",
      "css": ".ds-nav-shell{width:240px;padding:12px;background-color:var(--bg-sidebar,#ffffff);border:1px solid var(--border-sidebar,#e2e8f0);border-radius:12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;color:var(--text-sidebar,#475569);font:500 0.875rem/1.25 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 0.15s ease,color 0.15s ease}.ds-nav:hover{background-color:var(--bg-sidebar-hover,#f1f5f9);color:var(--text-sidebar-active,#0f172a)}.ds-nav-active{background-color:var(--bg-sidebar-active,#e2e8f0);color:var(--text-sidebar-active,#0f172a);font-weight:600}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bottom Nav Item",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "bottom-nav-item",
      "description": "Mobile navigation row: 22px SVG stroked at 1.8, 10px label, safe-area padding, active colors icon and label together.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-bottomnav\"><a class=\"ds-bnitem\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"14\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"14\" width=\"7\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1\"/></svg><span>Home</span></a><a class=\"ds-bnitem ds-bnitem-active\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 20h16a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V5a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v14a1 1 0 0 0 1 1z\"/><path d=\"M8 8h8M8 12h6M8 16h4\"/></svg><span>Highlights</span></a><a class=\"ds-bnitem\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20\"/><path d=\"M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z\"/></svg><span>Review</span></a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-bottomnav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-around;padding:6px 8px;background-color:var(--bg-sidebar,#ffffff);border-top:1px solid var(--border-sidebar,#e2e8f0);border-radius:0 0 12px 12px}.ds-bnitem{display:flex;flex:1;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:1px;padding:6px 10px 4px;border-radius:8px;color:var(--text-sidebar-muted,#94a3b8);font:500 0.625rem/1.3 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;transition:color 0.15s,background-color 0.15s}.ds-bnitem:hover{color:var(--text-sidebar-active,#0f172a);background-color:var(--bg-sidebar-hover,#f1f5f9)}.ds-bnitem-active{color:var(--text-sidebar-active,#0f172a)}.ds-bnitem svg{width:22px;height:22px;display:block}.ds-bnitem svg rect,.ds-bnitem svg path{stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.8;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Review Heatmap Cell",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "heatmap-cell",
      "description": "The only data visualization in the product and the only component allowed a saturated ramp. Scales 1.4 on hover.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-heat\"><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-1\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-2\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-3\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-0\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-4\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-2\"></span><span class=\"ds-heat-cell ds-heat-0\"></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-heat{display:flex;gap:3px;padding:12px;background-color:var(--bg-card,#ffffff);border:1px solid var(--border-card,#e2e8f0);border-radius:12px}.ds-heat-cell{width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:3px;transition:transform 0.1s ease,opacity 0.1s ease}.ds-heat-cell:hover{transform:scale(1.4);position:relative;z-index:5}.ds-heat-0{background-color:var(--bg-page-alt,#f1f5f9)}.ds-heat-1{background-color:#bbf7d0}.ds-heat-2{background-color:#4ade80}.ds-heat-3{background-color:#16a34a}.ds-heat-4{background-color:#15803d}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Reading Room",
    "overview": "Commonplace is a reading room, not a workspace. Every surface exists to hold text and then get out of the way: a page is a stack of pale cards on slate paper, one accent color for the thing you should do next, and text carrying everything else. Density is low on purpose. A class census across app/templates/*.html counts 233 uses of text-sm and 195 of text-muted against zero uses of any display or hero type - the interface speaks in one quiet mid-size voice.\n\nThe room is themeable by design, and that is the load-bearing property of the whole system. Six built-in themes (Modern, Reader, Dark, Glass, Contemporary, Contemporary Dark) are nothing but CSS custom-property overwrites of the same ~40 token names in app/static/themes.css, and a user can drop a seventh into data/themes/. No template names a color; the theme swap is one class on <body> (base.html:22). The frontmatter records the Modern values as the normative source, and the other five themes re-key the same variables.\n\nComponents are quietly tactile. Cards lift 2px on hover and take a soft shadow, buttons respond on press, the heatmap cell scales under the cursor - small answers that stay small, so a wall of thirty highlight cards still reads as a page rather than a dashboard. Motion runs 150ms for state, 250-350ms for entrances, and always eases out. The Glass theme is the single place the system permits literal light: translucent cards over deep navy, blurred at 16px, with a shadowed accent. That glow is a deliberate theme identity, not a house style.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One accent per theme, spent sparingly and only on the next action",
      "Six theme sheets sharing a single token vocabulary, plus user-droppable themes",
      "Quiet type scale: 14px body, no display face, uppercase reserved for 12px labels",
      "Flat surfaces at rest; elevation appears only as a response to state",
      "Mobile is a real second layout - fixed bottom nav, bottom sheets, swipe rows",
      "Text-first proportions: highlight text is the largest recurring type on any page"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "A theme declares exactly one accent. Anything that wants a second color argues for a state (hover, wash, border) instead of a hue, and no screen spends the accent on more than roughly a tenth of its pixels. Its scarcity is what makes the next action legible."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Six-Shelf Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "Every color decision has to resolve in all six themes. A literal hex inside a template is a bug, because the theme swap is a single class on the body and hard-coded color breaks it silently - in the theme nobody testing happens to be using."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Legible Ramp Rule",
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "Three steps carry text; the fourth does not. A caption that needs to be quieter than Margin Gray gets more space or a smaller role, never the decorative token - reaching past the last legible step is what put 2.6:1 text in the shell."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Line Rule",
        "section": "typography",
        "body": "Quoted material is serif where the theme offers one, set at 1.75 line-height, never smaller than 15px, and never truncated mid-sentence to make a card fit."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Uppercase Reserve Rule",
        "section": "typography",
        "body": "Uppercase belongs to labels and badges at 12px with 0.05em tracking. Titles, buttons, and navigation are sentence case."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-Until-Touched Rule",
        "section": "elevation",
        "body": "Surfaces are flat at rest. Shadows are a response to state - hover, focus, or an actual physical metaphor like a key cap - never a way to rank importance."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Exception Rule",
        "section": "elevation",
        "body": "Colored glow is fenced inside the Glass theme. No other theme gains a chromatic box-shadow or halo, because a glow that appears in one shelf has to be justified in all six."
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** define every color, border, and surface as a token in `app/static/themes.css` and consume it through `var()` or a semantic class. Six themes read the same variable names, so a token is what makes a change themeable at all.",
      "**Do** check any visual change in all six themes before calling it done - Modern, Reader, Dark, Glass, Contemporary, Contemporary Dark - since a low-contrast pair that passes on slate paper can fail on cream or on translucent glass.",
      "**Do** keep the accent rare. One action per view earns it; the rest belongs to type and surface.",
      "**Do** keep quoted material serif where the theme offers one, at 1.75 line-height and at least 15px.",
      "**Do** reuse the incumbent's tactile values - `translateY(-2px)` with `0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)`, press-scale 0.99 - so dozens of cards behave identically instead of each inventing its own lift.",
      "**Do** build mobile as its own layout (bottom nav, bottom sheets, swipe rows, safe-area padding) rather than shrinking the desktop column.",
      "**Do** keep UI edits portable to upstream `cansas/commonplace`; friction here is paid twice.",
      "**Do** theme the browser's own surfaces from the palette - caret, placeholder, selection, scrollbars, focus. They are the cheapest signal that a page was built rather than assembled: `caret-color: var(--color-accent)`, placeholders at `var(--text-muted)`, focus authored once as `outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent)`.",
      "**Do** draw icons as SVG in one stroke weight (1.8, round caps and joins) and mark them `aria-hidden`; the row label carries the meaning.",
      "**Do** give the accent's text-bearing pair to anything that puts text on the accent (`--btn-primary-bg` + `--btn-primary-text`), so a dark theme reads dark-on-amber instead of white-on-amber at 2.1:1.",
      "**Do** give a repeated literal a token before the third copy. Provenance, swipe actions, the heat ramp and the error surface were all extracted this pass; each had been a literal repeated across files, and the error surface had drifted into five different reds.",
      "**Do** confirm a token exists before referencing it. Seven `var()` references here pointed at names that were never defined (`--sidebar-muted`, `--sidebar-active`, `--sidebar-hover`, `--page-alt`, `--interactive-accent`), so the mobile bottom nav silently lost its colours and the review chart stayed indigo in all six themes. A missing token fails without a warning; check the name against `themes.css`.",
      "**Do** keep pre-auth and first-run surfaces on the same tokens as the app. `/setup` used to be a self-contained page with eleven hardcoded colours; it now links `themes.css` and reads every colour from tokens, so a new user's first screen follows the theme system instead of freezing the Modern palette."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** ship a second shade of a colour that already has a meaning. One danger set, one accent per theme, one ramp per data surface; a new shade is a new intent or a bug.",
      "**Don't** introduce a color literal outside `themes.css`. The theme swap is one class on `<body>` (`base.html:22`), and a hard-coded hex silently breaks the theme nobody happens to be testing. The three source-badge tints in `style.css:97-113` are the existing debt of this kind.",
      "**Don't** write Tailwind classes that need a config file. `tailwind.min.js` is the 3.4.17 Play CDN bundle with no config, so palette utilities like `ring-accent/40` and `accent-accent` resolve to nothing - which is why 37 call sites paired `focus:outline-none` with a ring that painted Tailwind's default blue. The project's own semantic classes (`.bg-accent`, `.text-primary`, `.border-card`) are the supported path. `themes.css` now maps `--tw-ring-color` to the accent so those call sites are correct until they are rewritten; new work should not add more of them.",
      "**Don't** check in a build step. The frontend is Jinja, hand-written CSS, a bundled Tailwind, and vanilla JS; parity with upstream depends on there being no npm toolchain.",
      "**Don't** add motion without a reduced-motion guard. `prefers-reduced-motion` appears nowhere in the codebase today, so every animation added widens that gap.",
      "**Don't** extend the Glass theme's glow, blur, or translucent cards into the other five themes. Glass is an identity, not a technique to borrow.",
      "**Don't** put emoji in chrome. Page copy may use one as a content glyph, but navigation, toggles, and badges use drawn SVG; emoji carry a different weight, color, and baseline on every platform, which is why the shell stopped using them.",
      "**Don't** introduce a display face or hero type. Hierarchy is bought with size, weight, and position in the existing scale."
    ]
  }
}